My previous best game was dying to Pestilence.
This game I had luck on top of luck on top of luck.

I found a wand of wishing (0:3) sitting in the open before oracle and
decided since I didn't have any artifacts yet that I would go for the
gusto. I wound up with Eye of Aethiopica, Staff of Aesculapius, Orb of
Fate, speed boots, SDSM.

I got BoH from sokobon (I wound up with 5 throughout the game). When I
went back to minetown around level 10 I got create familiar from the
shop and even though the failure rate was about 60% I couldn't resist
using it a few times. I wound up with a pet MMF that I named "The
Brain". He stuck with me until Gehennom when I was clearin a path with
my pickaxe and some brainless monster hacked him to death while I was
hacking walls.

I found a bones file on the oracle level with a few goodies including
Helm of Brilliance (well nice until I get my quest artifact). Continued
to lvl 12 and found a Cha priest and altar and let The Brain take him
out. Was able to convert it shortly thereafter and used this level as a
base for a long time. Wound up with Vorpal Blade and Demonbane and
blessed book of MM. YAY! Once I was done using up all my /oCM and ?oCM.
Also telepathy.

I continued and a few levels before castle I found another bones file
that a wizard of mine left wrapped up in a statue on the upstairs. I
think I did something dumb that game with a c corpse. This bones file
gave me doubles of most of my "kit" as well as Magicbane and
Greyswandir! Woo hoo. Also were lots more spellbooks, potions etc.

I found that my pet was so dang effective that I wound up delaying the
quest for a while since my level wasnt going up much. I would love to
see what he wound up killing. I went back to do the quest which wound
up being no problem as well as the Titan and Medusa and continued on to
the castle. I moved my base camp here and came back repeatedly.
Polypiled liberally here and got all kinds of goodies including =oT and
=oTC, a stack of 6 ?oG, more spellbooks. At this point I knew I was
very close to having a great game.

I Gehennom, some nasty lich summoned Juiblex in VotD which reminded me
how Demogorgon wasted my last "invincible" character. So geno'd those
right quick. Normally I would also get rid of MMF but my pet was just
too much fun. The Brain wound up equipped with a AoLS, Trident, misc
armor that got him down to -10ac and a UH. I took away the trident from
him and tried to force him to pick up Vorpy or Demonbane which he did,
but never wielded. For a short time he was in hell with a silver saber
until the fool dropped it somewhere for another trident. I let The
Brain eat all the wraith corpses we found and he wound up lvl 27 with
220hp and -10ac. At some point I also wound up with a Jabberwock pet
that I kept until planes of water.

So Juiblex died early, Hell was typically dull, though amazingly less
so with mapping and a +7 pickaxe. The one major annoyance was in Orcus
town when I didn't notice that a werewolf had infected me and a short
while later I lost half my armor when I turned into a wolf.
Fortunately, my pets protected me while the lycanthropy wore off and I
went back to the castle to fix my gear. Still had the castle wish wand
at (0:1) so I wasted two wishes to get it back up to snuff. I had one
wish left when I ascended and meant to use it on blessed figurine of
Archon, but forgot. Everything here went fine and according to plan  on
my long (actually short with T and TC) way back up.

Earth was easy, Air was easy, Water annoying as I even recharged OoF to
find the portal. As it turned out it was under a statue and I kept
missing it. Fire left me with my last real scare as something (fire
vortex?) swallowed me and when I killed it I found myself knee deep in
lava. Got out of this with CoC and Dig and then started cooling a path
to the portal. Not sure if I'm getting them out of order but oh well.
Wound up in astral plane with conflict and it seemed a ton easier to
kill those 4 angels than it did my one other time with a guardian
angel. I was able to move through much quicker without getting bogged
down by tons of summoning because they were all fighting each other.

